I learned about the various GitHub terminology, including a fork, branch, commit, pull request, and merge 
A fork involves duplicating a section of the base code wherein you can develop a branch of potential changes 
A commit will essentially confirm the changes you are seeking to realize in the base code 
Then, you can draft an official pull request which requests to MERGE the duplicated section of code to the base 
also READ MEs are incredibly helpful instruments to clairfy coding intentions 
